+# Harness sheet: DeepSeek Harness (how this runtime exposes the room)
+- Tools: the seat runs `dsh --profile acp` with `DSH_HOME` at its own runtime. Paseo talks to it over ACP and injects the room's MCP servers (`slp` and the Paseo agent tools; your role only allows some) into the session. Use the tool names they present. Do not conclude they are missing.
+- Skills: your role's `slp-*` skills are in this runtime's skills directory; read one when a procedure names it.
+- Off in this runtime: your own `cordis.patch.yml` is absent, so no user plugin layer loads; sessions and storages under this `DSH_HOME` are the seat's own. A denial is the room's rule, not an error to work around.
+- Modes: dsh has no Paseo session mode; a seat is created with none. Signing in is the `dsh` CLI's own sign-in, shared with every dsh seat.
